        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The committed-tree file listing included symlinks and gitlinks (submodules), while the working-tree listing correctly excluded them. Since a tracked symlink is stored as a blob whose content is the target path string, listing it as a source file would hand that path to the parser as if it were code. This divergence meant the graph could change shape depending on whether ",
