    "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nThe committed-tree file listing included symlinks and gitlinks (submodules), while the working-tree listing correctly excluded them. Since a tracked symlink is stored as a blob whose content is the target path string, listing it as a source file would hand that path to the parser as if it were code. This divergence meant the graph could change shape depending on whether --worktree was set.\nSolution:\nAdded ListRegularFiles() in gitutil to enumerate only regular files (modes 100644, 100755) from a committed tree, filtering out symlinks (120000), gitlinks (160000), and tree entries (040000) via their git ls-tree mode bits. Updated the committed-tree code path in provider.go to use this new function, achieving parity with the working-tree listing. Added regression tests confirming mode parsing and symlink exclusion, plus an end-to-end invariant test that committed and worktree snapshots agree on file membership. Bumped provider and search cache versions (records v8→v9, search-snapshot v12→v13) to invalidate prior cached results that contained spurious file records.",
